  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a 79-minute set at the Urban Lounge in Salt Lake City, Utah, on May 27, 2015 [1][2]. This recording, captured by LopsidedLolly, is the only available audio for this specific date [1]. The show opens with “Blood Capsules,” a track that appears in only eight archived performances [1][2]. The setlist includes “Cry for Judas,” “Animal Mask,” and “Foreign Object” [1]. “Going to Bolivia” is a notable inclusion, as it is the first appearance of the song in 64 archived shows and is considered rare with only 13 archived performances [2]. A “harsh noise component” follows, marking its first appearance in 39 archived shows [2]. “Heel Turn 2” is played, followed by “(i'm the main attraction),” which is also a first in 39 archived shows [2]. “Going to Norwalk” is a legendary track, as this is the only archived performance of it [2]. “(resentment at Disneyland)” appears next, also a first in 39 archived shows [2]. The set continues with “Woke Up New” and “Steal Smoked Fish” [1]. “(a jazzy song)” is another first in 39 archived shows [2]. “Fire Editorial” is rare, with only six archived performances [2]. “The Diaz Brothers,” “Luna,” “Stabbed to Death Outside San Juan,” and “Love Love Love” are performed [1]. “(LDS story)” is a first in 39 archived shows [2]. “Never Quite Free” and “Amy AKA Spent Gladiator 1” round out the main set [1]. The encore features “Up the Wolves” [1]. “(no children intro)” is a first in 39 archived shows [2]. “No Children” concludes the show [1]. Spoken introductions include a story about Dusty Rhodes [1]. This is the 205th show for the band in the archive [2].",
